# RecAbs: the record's dedupe at the level of landings, for S5 from record 9's I1 and I2.
RecAbs.cfg RecAbs expect=pass timeout=1800 why=S5 and IndInv on every reachable state (two writers of two ops, a name)
RecAbsCtlRaise.cfg RecAbs expect=violate:AtMostOnce timeout=600 why=control: record 4 steps 7 and 8, a drop that does not raise h
RecAbsCtlEntry.cfg RecAbs expect=violate:AtMostOnce timeout=600 why=control: record 4 step 5, cheapest's round 1 entry
ApaRecAbs.tla recabs-init-ConstInit expect=pass timeout=1800 tool=apalache args=--cinit=ConstInit --init=Init --next=Next --inv=IndInv --length=0 why=initiation: Init implies IndInv
ApaRecAbs.tla recabs-ind-ConstInit expect=pass timeout=3600 tool=apalache args=--cinit=ConstInit --init=IndInit --next=Next --inv=IndInv --length=1 why=consecution: I1 and I2 are inductive, so S5 holds in every state (two writers of two ops, two names)
ApaRecAbs.tla recabs-ind-ConstBig expect=pass timeout=14400 tool=apalache args=--cinit=ConstBig --init=IndInit --next=Next --inv=IndInv --length=1 why=consecution on three writers of three ops
ApaRecAbs.tla recabs-ind-CtlRaise expect=violate:IndInv timeout=1800 tool=apalache args=--cinit=CtlRaise --init=IndInit --next=Next --inv=IndInv --length=1 why=control: the induction needs the horizon raise
ApaRecAbs.tla recabs-ind-CtlEntry expect=violate:IndInv timeout=1800 tool=apalache args=--cinit=CtlEntry --init=IndInit --next=Next --inv=IndInv --length=1 why=control: the induction needs the entry rule
RecAbsProofs.tla - expect=proved timeout=3600 tool=tlapm why=TLAPS: IndInv (I1, I2 and the facts they rest on) is inductive for any writers, ops, names and stamps, so S5 AtMostOnce holds
